Lab 14: Optimizing Task Execution with Parallelism
Objectives

By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

    Understand the concept of parallel execution in Ansible playbooks
    Configure and implement parallel task execution using various Ansible strategies (linear, free, serial, async)
    Modify existing playbooks to leverage parallelism for improved performance
    Accurately measure and analyze performance improvements achieved through parallel execution
    Apply best practices for optimizing playbook execution time and troubleshoot common parallelism issues

Prerequisites

Before starting this lab, students should have:

    Basic understanding of Ansible playbooks, tasks, and modules
    Familiarity with YAML syntax and Ansible inventory management
    Experience writing and executing Ansible playbooks
    Knowledge of Linux command-line operations and SSH key-based authentication
    Completion of previous Ansible labs covering basic automation concepts

Required software (install on the control node if not already present):

sudo yum install -y ansible python3 python3-pip
pip3 install --user jc

